    "heightBasis": "Retained exact-QID OSM way712271284/Q1802388 matches current main35185084360116. All18 current raw whole-outline vertices/tags and two tile fragments reproduce by rigid rotation without rescale. Height/min_height and separate component controls are absent. Western projection is interpreted as bell tower/porch zone; wider eastern/southward church body carries the drum. Campanile separation/connection is not independently mapped and its internal partition is approximate within about3m. Church roof/porch partitions and12-sided drum center[2.5,-0.8]m/radius4.7m are picture estimates. Estimated levels: base5m, main walls9m/cross gables13.4m, porch walls6m/roof8.4m, low ranges6.5m/roof7.2m, drum12..21m/conical metal roof24.8m/cross25.8m. Bell tower lower6m, open middle6.5..11.5m, narrower upper12..16m/metal roof18.4m/cross19.2m. All vertical dimensions, fenestration, shallow geometric blind arcades/carved crosses/rosettes and porch/portal details are approximate. No surveyed height or engineering accuracy claimed.",
    "scope": "Individual Nikortsminda Cathedral: compact gray-tan stone church with cross-gabled silver metal roofs, tall12-sided narrow-slit drum/conical roof/cross, shallow round blind arcades with selected geometric crosses/rosettes and nested stone portal surrounds. Approximate western three-storey campanile with lower closed arched fields, open middle/narrower upper belfries, gray hipped roof/cross; lower porch and map-envelope ranges complete the body. Four existing shared ashlar/limestone/standing-seam metal/wood graphs, linear tints, metric UVs, flat architectural normals and four browser levels. Fine figurative carving/inscriptions/interlace, frescoes/full interiors/bells, hidden rear window/roof joins, exact tower separation and surveyed court/thresholds remain approximate or excluded."
